{
  "uid": "dpe-payments",
  "title": "DPE - Payments",
  "description": "Distributed payment engine, M6.\n\nPanels split three ways on purpose: RED for request-driven work, a section of its own for the saga (which is neither a request nor a resource), and USE for resources. Every panel description names the meter it reads. Panels reading dpe_* stay empty until those meters exist - this dashboard is the specification for them, not a decoration over them.",
  "tags": [
    "dpe",
    "payments",
    "m6"
  ],
  "timezone": "browser",
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "version": 1,
  "editable": true,
  "refresh": "10s",
  "time": {
    "from": "now-30m",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "templating": {
    "list": [
      {
        "name": "application",
        "label": "service",
        "type": "query",
        "datasource": {
          "type": "prometheus",
          "uid": "dpe-prometheus"
        },
        "query": {
          "query": "label_values(jvm_info, application)",
          "refId": "app"
        },
        "definition": "label_values(jvm_info, application)",
        "refresh": 1,
        "includeAll": true,
        "allValue": ".*",
        "multi": false,
        "current": {
          "text": "All",
          "value": "$__all"
        },
        "sort": 1
      }
    ]
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "type": "row",
      "title": "At a glance",
      "id": 1,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "collapsed": false,
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Transfers accepted /min",
      "description": "Rate of successful POST /api/v1/transfers. The business's own definition of throughput - not requests, not messages. 2xx only: a 422 is a request the system handled correctly and a payment that never happened.",
      "id": 2,
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "dpe-prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 5,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 1
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "dpe-prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum(rate(http_server_requests_seconds_count{application=\"payment-orchestrator\",uri=\"/api/v1/transfers\",method=\"POST\",status=~\"2..\"}[5m])) * 60",
          "legendFormat": "accepted/min",
          "range": true,
          "editorMode": "code"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "decimals": 1,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "graphMode": "area",
        "colorMode": "value",
        "textMode": "auto",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Compensation rate",
      "description": "COMPENSATED terminal sagas as a fraction of sagas started, over 5m.\n\nThe single most useful number on this dashboard. A compensated saga is NOT an error - the money went back, every invariant held, the system did exactly what it was built to do - so it appears in no error rate and no 5xx graph. This is the only place a degrading downstream PSP becomes visible before customers notice.\n\nMetrics: dpe.saga.terminal{status}, dpe.saga.started",
      "id": 3,
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "dpe-prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 5,
        "x": 5,
        "y": 1
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "dpe-prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum(rate(dpe_saga_terminal_total{application=\"payment-orchestrator\",status=\"COMPENSATED\"}[5m]))\n  / clamp_min(sum(rate(dpe_saga_started_total{application=\"payment-orchestrator\"}[5m])), 0.001)",
          "legendFormat": "compensated",
          "range": true,
          "editorMode": "code"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "decimals": 2,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "yellow",
                "value": 0.02
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 0.1
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "graphMode": "area",
        "colorMode": "value",
        "textMode": "auto",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Outbox backlog",
      "description": "Unpublished outbox rows across all three services.\n\nWhy backlog and not publish throughput: a relay that has STOPPED and a system with NO TRAFFIC produce the same throughput graph - zero. Backlog tells them apart. It is the difference between 'quiet' and 'broken', which is the first question in every incident.\n\nMetric: dpe.outbox.backlog",
      "id": 4,
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "dpe-prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 4,
        "x": 10,
        "y": 1
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "dpe-prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum(dpe_outbox_backlog)",
          "legendFormat": "rows",
          "range": true,
          "editorMode": "code"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "decimals": null,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "yellow",
                "value": 50
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 500
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "graphMode": "area",
        "colorMode": "value",
        "textMode": "auto",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Oldest unpublished row",
      "description": "Age of the oldest un-relayed outbox row anywhere.\n\nStrictly better than backlog as an alert: a large backlog that is draining is fine, a single row stuck for ten minutes is a broken relay. Depth measures volume, age measures progress.\n\nMetric: dpe.outbox.age (seconds)",
      "id": 5,
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "dpe-prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 4,
        "x": 14,
        "y": 1
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "dpe-prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "max(dpe_outbox_age_seconds)",
          "legendFormat": "oldest",
          "range": true,
          "editorMode": "code"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "decimals": null,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "yellow",
                "value": 30
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 120
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "graphMode": "area",
        "colorMode": "value",
        "textMode": "auto",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Dead letters",
      "description": "Unresolved rows in dead_letters, summed over services.\n\nNot a rate - a DEPTH, because a dead letter is not an event that passed, it is work still sitting there. Anything above zero is a human's queue.\n\nMetric: dpe.dlq.depth",
      "id": 6,
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "dpe-prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 3,
        "x": 18,
        "y": 1
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "dpe-prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum(dpe_dlq_depth)",
          "legendFormat": "messages",
          "range": true,
          "editorMode": "code"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "decimals": null,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "graphMode": "area",
        "colorMode": "value",
        "textMode": "auto",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Sagas in flight",
      "description": "Non-terminal sagas. Should return to zero after a burst; a floor that never comes back down is invariant I4 failing in slow motion, visible here long before verify-invariants.sh runs.\n\nMetric: dpe.saga.inflight{state}",
      "id": 7,
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "dpe-prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 3,
        "x": 21,
        "y": 1
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "dpe-prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum(dpe_saga_inflight{application=\"payment-orchestrator\"})",
          "legendFormat": "in flight",
          "range": true,
          "editorMode": "code"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "decimals": null,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "yellow",
                "value": 50
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 500
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "graphMode": "area",
        "colorMode": "value",
        "textMode": "auto",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Golden signals - RED (request-driven work)",
      "id": 8,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 5
      },
      "collapsed": false,
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Rate - requests by endpoint",
      "description": "Built in. http.server.requests comes from Boot with no code written; `uri` is the TEMPLATED path, which is what keeps this bounded - /api/v1/transfers/{id} is one series, not one per transfer. management.metrics.web.server.max-uri-tags=50 is the backstop if templating ever fails.",
      "id": 9,
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "dpe-prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 6
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "dpe-prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (uri, method) (rate(http_server_requests_seconds_count{application=\"$application\"}[1m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{method}} {{uri}}",
          "range": true,
          "editorMode": "code"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "reqps",
          "min": null,
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": true,
            "stacking": {
              "mode": "none",
              "group": "A"
            }
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true,
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull",
            "max"
          ]
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Errors - by outcome",
      "description": "Split rather than summed. CLIENT_ERROR is usually the caller's problem (a 422 for insufficient funds, a 403 for the wrong owner) and SERVER_ERROR is always ours; one blended ratio pages somebody at 3am because a client sent a bad request.",
      "id": 10,
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "dpe-prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 8,
        "y": 6
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "dpe-prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (outcome) (rate(http_server_requests_seconds_count{application=\"$application\",outcome!=\"SUCCESS\"}[1m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{outcome}}",
          "range": true,
          "editorMode": "code"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "reqps",
          "min": null,
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": true,
            "stacking": {
              "mode": "normal",
              "group": "A"
            }
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true,
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull",
            "max"
          ]
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Duration - p50 / p95 / p99",
      "description": "Computed from _bucket series by Prometheus, NOT from client-side percentiles.\n\nThis is why management.metrics.distribution.percentiles-histogram is set instead of `percentiles`: a percentile computed inside one JVM cannot be aggregated across instances - averaging two p99s produces a number that is not the p99 of anything. Buckets CAN be summed, so this query stays correct with three replicas behind a load balancer.",
      "id": 11,
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "dpe-prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 16,
        "y": 6
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "dpe-prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.50, sum by (le) (rate(http_server_requests_seconds_bucket{application=\"$application\"}[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "p50",
          "range": true,
          "editorMode": "code"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "dpe-prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le) (rate(http_server_requests_seconds_bucket{application=\"$application\"}[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "p95",
          "range": true,
          "editorMode": "code"
        },
        {
          "refId": "C",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "dpe-prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.99, sum by (le) (rate(http_server_requests_seconds_bucket{application=\"$application\"}[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "p99",
          "range": true,
          "editorMode": "code"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "min": null,
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 0,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": true,
            "stacking": {
              "mode": "none",
              "group": "A"
            }
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true,
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull",
            "max"
          ]
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "row",
      "title": "The saga - long-lived work, which is neither RED nor USE",
      "id": 12,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 14
      },
      "collapsed": false,
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Starts vs terminal outcomes",
      "description": "Sagas started against sagas reaching each terminal state. In steady state the lines meet; a persistent gap is work accumulating in flight.\n\nMetrics: dpe.saga.started, dpe.saga.terminal{status=COMPLETED|COMPENSATED|FAILED}",
      "id": 13,
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "dpe-prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 15
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "dpe-prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum(rate(dpe_saga_started_total{application=\"payment-orchestrator\"}[1m])) * 60",
          "legendFormat": "started",
          "range": true,
          "editorMode": "code"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "dpe-prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (status) (rate(dpe_saga_terminal_total{application=\"payment-orchestrator\"}[1m])) * 60",
          "legendFormat": "{{status}}",
          "range": true,
          "editorMode": "code"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "min": null,
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": true,
            "stacking": {
              "mode": "none",
              "group": "A"
            }
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true,
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull",
            "max"
          ]
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Saga duration by outcome - p50 / p95 / p99",
      "description": "Start to terminal state, which OUTLIVES the HTTP response - the request returns 202 while the saga is still running, so no request timer can measure this. Split by status on purpose: a COMPENSATED saga is legitimately slower than a COMPLETED one (it did strictly more work), and blending them hides both.\n\nMetric: dpe.saga.duration{status} - a Timer, with buckets enabled in application.yml",
      "id": 14,
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "dpe-prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 8,
        "y": 15
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "dpe-prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.50, sum by (le, status) (rate(dpe_saga_duration_seconds_bucket{application=\"payment-orchestrator\"}[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "p50 {{status}}",
          "range": true,
          "editorMode": "code"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "dpe-prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le, status) (rate(dpe_saga_duration_seconds_bucket{application=\"payment-orchestrator\"}[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "p95 {{status}}",
          "range": true,
          "editorMode": "code"
        },
        {
          "refId": "C",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "dpe-prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.99, sum by (le, status) (rate(dpe_saga_duration_seconds_bucket{application=\"payment-orchestrator\"}[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "p99 {{status}}",
          "range": true,
          "editorMode": "code"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "min": null,
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 0,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": true,
            "stacking": {
              "mode": "none",
              "group": "A"
            }
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true,
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull",
            "max"
          ]
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "In flight by state",
      "description": "A gauge over saga_instances grouped by state - the live version of invariant I4. STARTED piling up means replies are not arriving; RESERVED piling up means the gateway is not answering; COMPENSATING piling up means the release command is not landing. The SHAPE names the broken hop, which no single counter can do.\n\nMetric: dpe.saga.inflight{state}",
      "id": 15,
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "dpe-prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 16,
        "y": 15
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "dpe-prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (state) (dpe_saga_inflight{application=\"payment-orchestrator\"})",
          "legendFormat": "{{state}}",
          "range": true,
          "editorMode": "code"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "min": null,
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": true,
            "stacking": {
