    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Outbox backlog by service",
      "description": "COUNT of rows with published_at IS NULL, per service.\n\nA gauge like this runs a query on EVERY SCRAPE - every 10 seconds, forever, against a table on the write path of every payment. It must be an index-only count using the same partial index the relay itself uses, or the metric becomes a sequential scan that degrades the system it was added to observe. Measuring is not free.\n\nMetric: dpe.outbox.backlog",
      "id": 17,
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
